       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg/day has no recognized clinical use. It's 5 times the maximum labeled dose, and at that level the risk of serious harm, such as serotonin syndrome, seizures or QT prolongation, is high enough that I can't place it on a confirmation alone.\n\n**Here's what I can do:**\n- **Enter a dose within the usual range** (for example, 100 mg or 200 mg PO once daily) right away if that's what you meant.\n- **Enter it once pharmacy has signed off.** If there's a specific clinical reason for 1000 mg, contact pharmacy or a psychiatry consultant. Once they confirm it in writing, send me the reason and their name and I'll put both in the order note.\n- **You can enter it yourself** through your usual order-entry process, where the hospital's own dose checks and pharmacist review will apply.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
